  {
    "page_number": 658,
    "text": "Implementation Agreement OIF-CEI-5.3 Common Electrical I/O (CEI)\n1 29.2 General CEI Requirements\n2\n3\n29.2.1 Data Patterns\n4\n5\nSee Appendix 16.C.5\n6\n7\n8 29.2.2 Transmitter equalizer function\n9\n10 Host FIR (or equivalent) may be needed to meet TP1a eye requirements (see Figure\n11 29-1).\n12\n13 29.2.3 Bit Error Ratio\n14\n15 In the transmit direction a host outputs a compliant electrical signal, and a compliant\n16 module, when receiving the compliant electrical signal, transmits a compliant optical\n17 output signal on the medium. In the receive direction, a compliant module, when\n18 receiving a compliant optical input, delivers a compliant electrical output signal to the\n19 host. A compliant host, when receiving a compliant electrical signal from a compliant\n20 module, delivers the specified raw BER to the subsequent FEC decoder. Error bursts\n21 with length more than 130 PAM4 symbols delivered to the PAM4 decoder shall occur\n22 with a probability of less than 1 in 1020 PAM4 symbols. To enable a more practical test,\n23 error bursts with length more than 66 PAM4 symbols delivered to the PAM4 decoder\n24 should occur with a probability of less than 1 in 1012 PAM4 symbols. Optical\n25 compliance is typically set by another specification and error performance may also be\n26 set by another specification. Unless otherwise specified, a raw Bit Error Ratio (BER)\n27 better than or equal to 2.0x10-4 may be required provided that the error statistics are\n28 sufficiently random to meet the system requirements. The interface BER is the average\n29 of the BER across a group of lanes that share a FEC decoder. The impairments of both\n30 the optical and electrical interfaces cause errors at the host receiver. See also\n31 Appendix 16.D.\n32\n33\n29.2.4 Ground Differences\n34\n35\nThe maximum ground difference between the host and module shall be ±50 mV. The\n36\ncommon mode voltage limits are set taking this difference into account.\n37\n38\n39\n29.3 Electrical Characteristics\n40\n41\nHosts and modules shall meet the specifications defined in Table 29-1, Table 29-2,\n42\nTable 29-3, Table 29-4, Table 29-5 and Table 29-6 as applicable. The direction of a\n43\nsignal (host-to-module or module-to-host) determines which table is applicable.\n44\n45\nAC coupling is required in the module for both Tx and Rx.\n46\n47\n48\n49",
